WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 line:0% align:end size:15%
<ruby><rt>kaa.lt</rt></ruby>

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.894 
Even without a form...

00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:21.271 
We will never stop walking.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:38.288 
Looks like the cleanup is finally
just about over.

00:00:43.669 --> 00:00:46.922 
Once we finish laying
the cobblestones in one more area,

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:49.049 
we'll be done for the time being.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.180 
Has it been
ten years already?

00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:58.016 
Took some time, but...

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:02.145 
I'd say we bounced back fairly well
from that disaster.

00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:06.942 
Head Captain!

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:10.821 
We don't have any more time!
Please hurry up!

00:01:11.405 --> 00:01:12.489 
Good grief.

00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:16.285 
Still not used to how busy
being Head Captain is.

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.787 
Now I know how great
Old Man Yama was.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.960 
Well, I'll stop by again, Ukitake.

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.254 
UKITAKE

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.464 
Head Captain!

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:32.050 
All right!
I'm on my way!

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:44.021 
THE CALAMITY

00:01:45.897 --> 00:01:48.482 
<i>I've lived my way full of shame</i>

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:52.862 
<i>"Envy" comes from the ways
of the eventual end</i>

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:55.406 
<i>The ambiguous balance</i>

00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:58.243 
<i>I want to cut ties at once</i>

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.078 
<i>It's too late to back down now</i>

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:02.330 
<i>Before this senile body dies</i>

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:04.081 
<i>My shadow will fade away soon, but</i>

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:06.168 
<i>Even if I disappear, my journey won't stop</i>

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:07.793 
<i>Uncertain days, certain endings</i>

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.462 
<i>My stories fill the in-betweens</i>

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:12.214 
<i>Beyond the wall blocking my way,
there is a calm morning</i>

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:16.511 
<i>Like the rising sun,
I stand with the wind at my back</i>

00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:20.723 
<i>A burst of hope?</i>

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.975 
<i>Break through an endless night</i>

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:27.980 
<i>Show the sun waiting
at the end of darkness</i>

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.025 
<i>The promise is yet to be fulfilled</i>

00:02:31.026 --> 00:02:34.612 
<i>but I stand in solitude not to let it go</i>

00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:37.490 
<i>At the moment,
I'm connecting numerous lights</i>

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:41.203 
<i>to form a constellation
that paves tomorrow</i>

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.748 
<i>Even if the rain clouds
hide the night sky away</i>

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:49.211 
<i>there certainly is a flame in my heart</i>

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:54.383 
<i>God is no longer reliable</i>

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:59.262 
<i>I glance up towards the silver lining</i>

00:02:59.388 --> 00:03:05.601 
<i>The destiny of bursting fate</i>

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:07.979 
BLEACH THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:29.126 
Is West 55 District finally going
to be completed?

00:03:29.668 --> 00:03:32.462 
Took them long enough...

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:38.385 
I can finally expand my secret
network across all of Seireitei.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.095 
Now then...

00:03:40.429 --> 00:03:43.306 
Let's go do a field survey.

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:45.976 
Come with me!
Nemuri No. 8!

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.145 
Yes, Master Mayuri!

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.313 
Keep your voice down.

00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:52.941 
Yes! I'm sorry, Master Mayuri!

00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:55.110 
Good grief...

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.362 
How on earth did you
end up like this?

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:00.449 
I wonder why that is,
Master Mayuri!

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.076 
Thank you for today,
Captain Zaraki!

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.620 
Thank you for your hard work
today, Sir!

00:04:06.621 --> 00:04:07.538 
Thank you, Sir!

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:08.832 
Oh shut up!

00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:11.042 
It's the middle of the day—
I'm not done yet!

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.796 
You're right!
We're sorry!

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:16.798 
Have a nice day, Captain Zaraki.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.384 
- Have a nice day!
- Have a nice day!

00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:20.802 
By the way, Captain...

00:04:21.219 --> 00:04:23.346 
Isn't it at the Squad One's
barracks today?

00:04:23.805 --> 00:04:25.015 
Are we going the right way?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.517 
What are you talking about?

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.351 
Squad Thirteen is in charge,

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:31.313 
so it's going to be at
Squad Thirteen's barracks.

00:04:32.439 --> 00:04:34.232 
It's at Squad One's barracks, right?

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:36.735 
I don't know.
I'm only the Third Seat.

00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:38.653 
Get your act together.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.572 
Listen, Ikkaku...

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:45.202 
First of all, it was Yachiru's
fault that I got lost a lot.

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:47.370 
Now that Yachiru ain't here...

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.124 
There's no way I'd get lost!

00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:54.669 
Don't look at me!

00:04:55.086 --> 00:04:57.547 
I think the Captain's right!

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.799 
Now that we're all clear,
let's get going!

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.092 
Don't fall behind!

00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:04.429 
- Wait for us, Captain!
- Wait for us, Captain!

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:07.432 
That's Squad Eleven...

00:05:07.724 --> 00:05:09.601 
Why are they headed
the wrong way?

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.478 
Maybe they're lost?

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:14.940 
They're moving too fast to be lost.

00:05:15.106 --> 00:05:16.608 
I'll go and stop them.

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:18.276 
Oh, no way!
Don't do it!

00:05:18.652 --> 00:05:21.947 
What would we do if we get dragged
into their mess and end up late?

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.280 
But...

00:05:23.281 --> 00:05:25.033 
No ifs, ands or buts!

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.285 
They're grown adults—leave 'em be!

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.955 
Captain's orders!

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:32.498 
Captain Hirako...

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:35.669 
You only pull rank
when it doesn't matter...

00:05:35.877 --> 00:05:37.045 
Ah...

00:05:37.212 --> 00:05:39.381 
We have different values!

00:05:39.506 --> 00:05:41.675 
I don't pull rank
when it doesn't matter—

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.969 
I pull rank when I wanna!

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.770 
I can't do that, Captain!

00:05:54.062 --> 00:05:54.980 
Don't worry about it!

00:05:55.313 --> 00:05:56.898 
You guys catch up later!

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.984 
Straight to work from
the training grounds?

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.986 
You're working hard every day,
Captain Iba.

00:06:01.987 --> 00:06:03.154 
Captain Hitsugaya!

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:04.573 
No...

00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:07.409 
I still don't feel like
I'm captain material.

00:06:08.159 --> 00:06:09.744 
I feel like
if I skip a day training,

00:06:10.412 --> 00:06:12.873 
SEVEN
I won't be a captain anymore.

00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:15.417 
I see...

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.797 
That's admirable.

00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:24.676 
That could be what it takes
to be a captain.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.304 
I wish a certain someone
could hear that.

00:06:27.721 --> 00:06:30.849 
Who could that be?
Could it be Shuhei?

00:06:31.016 --> 00:06:31.892 
Sounds about right.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:33.602 
You should listen, Shuhei.

00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:35.979 
I can't let that slide, Rangiku.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:37.313 
For your information...

00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:40.942 
your captain agrees with us.

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:42.777 
Well, I'll have you know...

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:46.239 
I've mastered my Bankai
a long time ago.

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:49.034 
Well, I haven't actually seen it.

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:50.201 
Neither have I.

00:06:50.368 --> 00:06:52.661 
Sounds like you're all talk
and no Bankai.

00:06:52.662 --> 00:06:53.955 
I haven't see it either.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.875 
That's not true!
You've seen it, Captain.

00:06:57.375 --> 00:06:59.669 
W-What am I supposed to do?!

00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:02.297 
I haven't had a chance to use it
since that time!

00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:03.547 
Making excuses now?

00:07:03.548 --> 00:07:04.506 
That's an excuse...

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:06.718 
Stop taking their side, Captain!

00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:10.638 
Well, the fact that you haven't
had to use it in ten years

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:12.182 
is a good thing, right?

00:07:13.183 --> 00:07:17.062 
It means we've maintained peace
for ten years.

00:07:20.982 --> 00:07:22.984 
And to close out those ten years...

00:07:23.485 --> 00:07:26.528 
ONE
Today's ceremony is quite fitting,
I think.

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:27.030 
ONE

00:07:27.364 --> 00:07:29.157 
You're late!
What were you doing?!

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.158 
Huh?!

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:33.369 
We took a lap around Seireitei.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.038 
I think we got here early.

00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:38.749 
I'm asking why you took a lap
around Seireitei

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.460 
on an important day like today?!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.797 
All right, okay...

00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:47.049 
Why don't we all go inside!

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.968 
Please...

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:55.308 
Big Sis, you're a captain yourself,

00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:57.477 
don't be so intimidated by them!

00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:59.479 
Don't ask the impossible.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.481 
So the answer is no?

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:05.735 
This new song for the ceremony
will bring tears to your eyes.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:06.861 
No.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.655 
Please leave that here
and come with me.

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:11.199 
I brought the stage light.

00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:13.702 
Please leave that here
and come with me.

00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:18.415 
Lieutenant Ise is becoming
more authoritative with each year.

00:08:18.581 --> 00:08:21.543 
We'll be using this again
at tonight's reception.

00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:22.585 
For sure.

00:08:23.628 --> 00:08:24.462 
Well, then...

00:08:24.713 --> 00:08:26.297 
We will now begin the ceremony

00:08:26.631 --> 00:08:28.967 
to appoint a new captain
to Thirteen Court Guard Squads!

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.929 
Newly appointed Captain,
you may now enter!

00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:35.807 
What's with that face?

00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:37.016 
Don't sweat it.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.768 
If you freeze up
and twist your ankle,

00:08:38.893 --> 00:08:40.353 
I'll carry you on my shoulders.

00:08:40.687 --> 00:08:41.896 
S-Shut up...!

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:48.403 
Captain of Squad Thirteen:
Rukia Kuchiki!

00:08:48.778 --> 00:08:49.654 
Yes!

00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:51.238 
ONE

00:08:51.239 --> 00:08:51.780 
ONE
Huh?
Where did the Captain go?

00:08:51.781 --> 00:08:53.616 
Huh?
Where did the Captain go?

00:08:53.908 --> 00:08:55.410 
Oh, that's right...

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:58.038 
Today's that new captain-thingy.

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:01.750 
No, I think he went to survey
the recovery zone.

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:03.125 
Why is he doing that?

00:09:03.126 --> 00:09:04.626 
You're his lieutenant.

00:09:04.627 --> 00:09:06.629 
If you don't know
how am I supposed to know?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.506 
Good grief...

00:09:08.673 --> 00:09:11.092 
Fine, I'll go call him.

00:09:11.509 --> 00:09:12.802 
Did something happen?

00:09:13.011 --> 00:09:16.347 
Well, the instruments are
picking up a strange reading.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.391 
It's really similar to

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.728 
Yhwach's Spiritual Pressure
from ten years ago...

00:09:37.035 --> 00:09:38.327 
- Hey, hey!
- What?

00:09:38.328 --> 00:09:39.620 
What do you wanna do
at home?

00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:41.413 
Hmm... What should we do?
Video games!

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:43.582 
- That sounds great!
- Doesn't it?

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:45.668 
But wait,
you're really good at 'em so...

00:09:46.669 --> 00:09:47.962 
You know it!

00:09:55.386 --> 00:09:58.264 
UNAGIYA

00:10:03.228 --> 00:10:06.189 
Hey! What are you
doing there, lil' brat?!

00:10:06.481 --> 00:10:08.149 
How'd you get in here?

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.276 
What the—?

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.445 
Whatta speedy little bugger...

00:10:16.157 --> 00:10:18.117 
The Spiritual Pressure signature
believed to be

00:10:18.118 --> 00:10:19.576 
the remnants of
Yhwach's power...

00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:20.912 
is located in
West 55 District.

00:10:21.079 --> 00:10:24.165 
It's the last restoration section adjacent
to Squad Thirteen's barracks!

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:25.917 
Kuchiki!

00:10:26.918 --> 00:10:29.002 
The captain of Squad Thirteen
seems to have departed

00:10:29.003 --> 00:10:30.547 
right after the ceremony,

00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:32.215 
so I sent you out, but...

00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:33.508 
It's fine.

00:10:33.675 --> 00:10:35.969 
Rukia and the others haven't
had time off in a while.

00:10:36.678 --> 00:10:38.096 
There's no need to contact them.

00:10:38.596 --> 00:10:39.681 
I'll take care of this.

00:10:40.431 --> 00:10:41.266 
Oh?

00:10:41.558 --> 00:10:42.559 
That's odd.

00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:45.895 
I don't recall relaying any info
to you two.

00:10:46.187 --> 00:10:49.149 
Don't underestimate
the Stealth Force's intel network.

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:53.403 
The fact that you're here means
the intel was accurate.

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:55.071 
Oh boy...

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:56.823 
Accurate or not...

00:10:57.574 --> 00:10:59.909 
You'll see it for yourself
soon enough.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.420 
KUROSAKI CLINIC

00:11:11.296 --> 00:11:12.172 
Hey!

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:13.715 
Hey!

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:17.594 
Still no patients, I see!

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:18.928 
It's empty!

00:11:19.137 --> 00:11:21.598 
An empty clinic is a good thing.

00:11:21.764 --> 00:11:23.933 
Shut up and come in.

00:11:24.184 --> 00:11:25.685 
Everybody's here.

00:11:26.561 --> 00:11:29.522 
Oh! It's Rukia!
Make yourself at home, Rukia!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.442 
This isn't your house!

00:11:32.984 --> 00:11:34.194 
It's been so long, Rukia.

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:36.696 
Your hair's long!
It looks good!

00:11:36.905 --> 00:11:38.780 
Move it, Big Brother!

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:40.950 
Popcorn and cola coming through!!

00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:45.538 
Rukia! Long time no see!

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:47.582 
It's been so long
since I've seen you both!

00:11:47.749 --> 00:11:48.958 
You two have grown so much!

00:11:49.334 --> 00:11:50.793 
Okay, it's going to start!

00:11:51.002 --> 00:11:53.503 
- Ichigo, come sit over here!
- <i>Y-Hans presents!</i>

00:11:53.504 --> 00:11:56.507 
- <i>The world heavyweight title match!</i>
- Oh! There he is!

00:11:57.842 --> 00:12:00.470 
Isn't Chad incredible, though?

00:12:00.637 --> 00:12:03.806 
He ended up becoming
the most famous of all of us!

00:12:04.098 --> 00:12:06.016 
Does "us" include you?

00:12:06.017 --> 00:12:08.144 
That's what "us" means!

00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:12.272 
Where's Dr. Ishida?

00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:14.359 
He's on the roof taking
an extended break.

00:12:14.567 --> 00:12:16.526 
That's unusual, he doesn't do that...

00:12:16.527 --> 00:12:19.405 
Seems he couldn't get the day off.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:22.157 
ATTENDING PHYSICIAN
DR. URYU ISHIDA
He said there was a program
he was supposed to watch

00:12:22.158 --> 00:12:24.201 
with his friends
that he simply couldn't miss.

00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:26.204 
Oh, that's such a cute reason!

00:12:29.582 --> 00:12:30.959 
<i>See?! We're connected.</i>

00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:32.460 
<i>Oh, you there?</i>

00:12:32.794 --> 00:12:35.672 
What? Sounds like
you didn't want me to pick up.

00:12:35.964 --> 00:12:39.133 
No! You said you couldn't
take time off,

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.219 
so we were saying
we shouldn't bother you.

00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:45.765 
I can't leave the hospital,
but I was able to make some time.

00:12:46.683 --> 00:12:48.768 
I'll watch Sado's fight from here.

00:12:49.227 --> 00:12:50.143 
<i>Okay.</i>

00:12:50.144 --> 00:12:52.605 
<i>Ishida!
You doing all right?</i>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.315 
<i>Hey, don't interrupt!</i>

00:12:55.984 --> 00:12:57.901 
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:12:57.902 --> 00:12:59.654 
<i>Hey, it's not my fault!</i>

00:12:59.904 --> 00:13:01.155 
<i>What's so funny?</i>

00:13:01.531 --> 00:13:03.199 
It's nothing.

00:13:03.574 --> 00:13:04.659 
That's how it should be.

00:13:04.993 --> 00:13:07.537 
Always with
the cryptic comment, huh?

00:13:07.662 --> 00:13:09.289 
<i>You're one to talk.</i>

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:12.249 
Oh! Chad's on!

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.084 
Oh!

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:15.420 
<i>That's my cue!
I'm going to hang up now.</i>

00:13:15.837 --> 00:13:16.713 
<i>Later, Ishida!</i>

00:13:16.921 --> 00:13:17.880 
CALL ENDED
Hey, Kurosaki!

00:13:19.173 --> 00:13:21.175 
What's with that guy?

00:13:23.845 --> 00:13:25.680 
It's about to start, Orihime.

00:13:26.514 --> 00:13:27.557 
Okay!

00:13:28.099 --> 00:13:28.974 
<i>A tiger!</i>

00:13:28.975 --> 00:13:31.936 
<i>- Become a real tiger, Yasutora!
- Yes!</i>

00:13:32.353 --> 00:13:35.481 
Wow! Sado is really fired up!

00:13:36.149 --> 00:13:37.650 
He's definitely going to win. right?

00:13:37.817 --> 00:13:38.651 
Yeah.

00:13:39.444 --> 00:13:40.320 
Where's Kazui?

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.864 
Um... Upstairs right now.

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.116 
According to Tsubaki
and the others,

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:48.828 
he was just at Hiyori's place.

00:13:49.454 --> 00:13:50.997 
Maybe he's in your room, Big Bro...

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:52.999 
Kazu likes it there.

00:13:53.624 --> 00:13:55.084 
That's your room now.

00:13:55.293 --> 00:13:56.127 
You okay with that?

00:13:56.377 --> 00:13:58.796 
Of course! Kazu's always welcome.

00:13:59.005 --> 00:14:01.507 
It's 'cuz Kazu is
the spitting image of you, Ichigo.

00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:02.759 
Karin!

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.762 
Which reminds me,

00:14:06.054 --> 00:14:08.389 
didn't you guys say you were
bringing your kid this time?

00:14:08.723 --> 00:14:09.599 
Oh, right!

00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:12.393 
She's finally
a Court Guard Cadet now!

00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:15.521 
She was granted a travel permit
for the Obon holidays.

00:14:16.147 --> 00:14:17.315 
C'mon, get in here!

00:14:20.693 --> 00:14:23.070 
Yep.
Guess she's gone!

00:14:23.071 --> 00:14:23.988 
How does that happen?!

00:14:24.822 --> 00:14:26.031 
Good grief.

00:14:26.032 --> 00:14:28.367 
I told you we don't have to
look for her.

00:14:28.493 --> 00:14:29.744 
So how does this happen?!

00:14:30.161 --> 00:14:32.246 
KUROSAKI CLINIC
Relax. She's a Soul Reaper.

00:14:32.622 --> 00:14:34.373 
KUROSAKI CLINIC
No human's going to hurt her!

00:14:34.624 --> 00:14:36.959 
KUROSAKI CLINIC
Is she the type that picks fights
with humans?!

00:14:37.251 --> 00:14:38.628 
Then that's all the more reason...

00:14:39.462 --> 00:14:40.296 
Ichigo.

00:14:40.463 --> 00:14:41.339 
What?

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:45.760 
Looking back,
this is where it all started...

00:14:50.598 --> 00:14:52.141 
<i>Give me that sword, Soul Reaper.</i>

00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:54.727 
<i>Let's go with your idea!</i>

00:14:55.978 --> 00:14:57.230 
<i>My name is not "Soul Reaper."</i>

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:58.898 
<i>I am Rukia Kuchiki.</i>

00:14:59.732 --> 00:15:00.608 
<i>That so...</i>

00:15:01.192 --> 00:15:02.819 
<i>I'm Ichigo Kurosaki.</i>

00:15:03.861 --> 00:15:07.615 
<i>Let's pray this introduction
isn't our last.</i>

00:15:13.454 --> 00:15:14.330 
<i>Let's go.</i>

00:15:14.497 --> 00:15:15.373 
<i>Right.</i>

00:15:52.493 --> 00:15:55.913 
KUROSAKI CLINIC

00:15:56.497 --> 00:15:59.167 
Looking back,
we've come really far...

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.711 
Okay, let's go back...

00:16:02.128 --> 00:16:03.546 
to where everyone's waiting for us.

00:16:03.754 --> 00:16:04.630 
Yeah...

00:16:05.548 --> 00:16:07.842 
After we find your kid.

00:16:09.051 --> 00:16:10.927 
Stop sighing. It's your kid!

00:16:10.928 --> 00:16:12.721 
Hey, the fight's about to start.

00:16:12.722 --> 00:16:14.681 
Get out here and help us look.

00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:15.766 
Right. You, too!

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:18.519 
Oh! She's back.

00:16:18.895 --> 00:16:20.605 
Is that what that
Spiritual Pressure was?

00:16:21.189 --> 00:16:22.857 
- All right, let's go watch!
- Oh, hey!

00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:24.775 
- Go!
- Looking good!

00:16:24.942 --> 00:16:27.528 
- That's it! Get him!
- Offense! Offense!

00:16:39.916 --> 00:16:41.459 
It's coming!
Fall back!

00:16:44.754 --> 00:16:45.630 
What?!

00:16:46.088 --> 00:16:48.423 
The remnants of Yhwach's power...

00:16:48.424 --> 00:16:49.467 
...vanished?!

00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:57.975 
So the last of Yhwach's power...

00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:00.394 
is finally gone...

00:17:04.106 --> 00:17:05.149 
<i>The path...</i>

00:17:05.358 --> 00:17:07.193 
<i>has been sealed, Ichigo.</i>

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:10.738 
<i>The path to a world without fear.</i>

00:17:12.323 --> 00:17:17.035 
<i>The World of the Living,
the Soul Society, and Hueco Mundo...</i>

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:19.288 
<i>They should have become one.</i>

00:17:20.081 --> 00:17:24.835 
<i>Life and death were meant
to be combined into one.</i>

00:17:26.087 --> 00:17:29.382 
<i>But that can no longer be...</i>

00:17:31.717 --> 00:17:34.804 
<i>Thanks to you, Ichigo.</i>

00:17:36.264 --> 00:17:37.181 
<i>How disappointing.</i>

00:17:37.974 --> 00:17:39.267 
<i>Because of you,</i>

00:17:39.517 --> 00:17:41.852 
<i>life and death will retain
their shapes...</i>

00:17:42.144 --> 00:17:44.230 
<i>and all that has life</i>

00:17:44.605 --> 00:17:49.068 
<i>will continue to live in
constant fear of death now.</i>

00:17:50.945 --> 00:17:53.114 
<i>Forever.</i>

00:17:56.951 --> 00:17:57.952 
Yhwach.

00:17:58.494 --> 00:18:00.454 
Fear certainly
would not have existed

00:18:00.997 --> 00:18:02.748 
in the world you wished for.

00:18:03.791 --> 00:18:06.544 
But, in a world
without the fear of death,

00:18:07.253 --> 00:18:10.965 
people will not search for hope.

00:18:12.675 --> 00:18:16.220 
People will persist simply
by being alive.

00:18:16.971 --> 00:18:20.473 
But persistence
while fending off fear

00:18:20.474 --> 00:18:21.892 
is something completely different.

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:27.773 
That is why people have
a special name for it.

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.069 
They call it courage.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:38.326 
Who's there?

00:18:38.618 --> 00:18:41.746 
Ichika Abarai, Soul Reaper cadet!

00:18:42.163 --> 00:18:43.789 
ICHIKA ABARAI

00:18:43.998 --> 00:18:44.874 
Who are you?

00:18:45.708 --> 00:18:48.502 
I'm Kazui Kurosaki.

00:18:51.172 --> 00:18:52.798 
I'm a Soul Reaper, too.

00:18:53.215 --> 00:18:55.009 
KAZUI KUROSAKI

00:18:55.426 --> 00:18:56.344 
Huh?!

00:21:47.306 --> 00:21:48.598 
<i>Retracing memories</i>

00:21:48.599 --> 00:21:52.310 
<i>An unexpected gaze</i>

00:21:52.311 --> 00:21:54.813 
<i>The world I didn't want</i>

00:21:54.814 --> 00:21:56.815 
<i>I've started breaking it down</i>

00:21:56.816 --> 00:21:59.442 
<i>Lean on each other and face forward</i>

00:21:59.443 --> 00:22:02.071 
<i>I want to change my fate</i>

00:22:02.196 --> 00:22:05.323 
<i>All the voices shout</i>

00:22:05.324 --> 00:22:07.451 
<i>The sound rang out</i>

00:22:22.883 --> 00:22:25.426 
<i>I saw countless scattered shadows</i>

00:22:25.427 --> 00:22:27.763 
<i>and I laughed</i>

00:22:27.888 --> 00:22:30.223 
<i>A world that's lost its color</i>

00:22:30.224 --> 00:22:32.600 
<i>I'll illuminate it again</i>

00:22:32.601 --> 00:22:35.270 
<i>Broken and lamenting</i>

00:22:35.271 --> 00:22:37.897 
<i>The end of the dream</i>

00:22:37.898 --> 00:22:42.402 
<i>Shaking free from it over and over again
with a still-connected heart</i>

00:22:42.403 --> 00:22:48.074 
<i>I'll protect today,
the path I've walked all this time</i>

00:22:48.075 --> 00:22:49.118 
<i>Break it</i>

00:22:49.285 --> 00:22:51.744 
<i>Tear the future apart, call my name</i>

00:22:51.745 --> 00:22:54.747 
<i>Turn your back on your predetermined past</i>

00:22:54.748 --> 00:22:57.625 
<i>Today keeps playing with fate</i>

00:22:57.626 --> 00:22:59.669 
<i>Reclaim it here and now</i>

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:02.297 
<i>To the ends of the earth, an unseen dream</i>

00:23:02.298 --> 00:23:05.091 
<i>With eyes that know the strength
that lies in words</i>

00:23:05.092 --> 00:23:08.136 
<i>Notice the distorted spiral</i>

00:23:08.137 --> 00:23:12.099 
<i>My fate has been set in motion</i>